there's a very good article on medium by  a guy named Eric Medlen which talks a  lot about the upcoming midterm elections  but it also points out that there are  these three recent stories that have  gotten a lot of attention in the United  States two of which have been pushed  hugely by right-wing media one of which  has been reported on correctly by all  media but still all three of these  stories are potentially huge  distractions from the fact that we can  start going in the direction of fixing a  lot of the problems we're experiencing  right now merely by voting on Tuesday  and I want to be really clear here  because sometimes Pat when we say a  story is a distraction people hear that  it means it's not an important story and  that's not what we mean by a story is a  distraction and also even when we say a  story is a distraction that doesn't mean  that it's a deliberate distraction by  someone in pushing or talking about that  story so let me give you an example  Trump's fake tax cut this has been kind  of going around for several weeks now  you might not even have heard of it  because many shows haven't covered it  because it's fake and the idea is that  Trump floated that the Republican Party  may Doohan other-- tax cut so-called tax  cut I mean a lot of people's taxes  weren't actually cut by the first tax  cut that they may do another tax bill  which he's calling a tax cut by the end  of 2018 it's not gonna happen like it's  it's just it's simply not going to  happen if you look at the fact that the  midterms are next week and then you've  got a lame-duck session and you have  end-of-year breaks for lawmakers and the  fact that there is no such bill in  progress at this point in any state that  would be remotely close to actually be  voted on to be debated voted on in past  in 2018 it's totally fake okay and  Donald Trump talks about this at rallies  all the time like it's some kind of  imminent tax cut it does not exist okay  it's not gonna happen if indeed  Republicans keep control of the house  maybe they will pass another tax bill in  2019 or 2020 but there is no imminent  bill right now the way Donald Trump is  trying to claim it is a distraction and  even discussing the  merits of another tax cut could serve to  distract from the reality that people  just need to go vote between now and  Tuesday  okay Story number two the immigrant  Caravan this is a real story in the  sense that it exposes the underlying  xenophobia and in many cases sort of  nationalistic jingoism that exists on  the right they are selling it to us as  this imminent invasion of criminals  coming in to flood the United States to  commit crimes to rape women but the  reality is there's no invasion this is a  group of people seeking asylum it's a  group whose size is dwindling every  single day as they get closer to the  us-mexico border even Shepard Smith on  Fox News said nothing is happening and  if this actually did become a so-called  attempt to overrun the border that we  have huge law enforcement and it's just  not going to be a big deal it's nothing  nothing is happening does that mean we  should ignore the story because it's not  happening no we actually need to push  back against the talking points related  to the story but you've got to remember  that if Democrats go out and take  control of the house and take control of  how government money is spent all of a  sudden we retake a lot of the control  over how government resources are used  when it comes to immigrants number three  we talked about Trump's idea that was  learned about over the weekend of ending  birthright citizenship by executive  order it's a real story  I believe that Trump genuinely wants to  do it but it's not happening before the  election it's not at all likely that you  even can do this via executive order but  what do all three of these stories have  in common they are distractions from the  fact that your vote Tuesday can change  the direction of the country it's really  important to understand this Pat because  I feel like this is where people  sometimes lose the thread a story  doesn't have to be a deliberately  planted ploy to distract to effectively  serve as a distraction and that is what  I am trying to  people it doesn't mean every single one  of these stories is crafted as a  distraction we can't let our eye be  taken off the ball and that's why iPad  have just been talking every single day  lately about you've got to go vote  because that will give us way more  control over all of these issues then  talking about the stories now and you  can't help but think if these  distractions are going to work my  instinct is that the birthright  citizenship stuff and the migrant  caravan stuff isn't going to necessarily  sway independent voters I think that the  people who are in support of Trump are  going to stick by him but he's not gonna  pull over any people in the middle to  vote for Republicans in the midterm  elections based on those two issues the  middle-class tax cut thing maybe that  could sway some independence people who  aren't so knowledgable of the fact that  Congress isn't even in session right now  but they'll take Trump at its at his  word that I think could be effective now  all of that being said we do need to  understand that number one increasingly  it doesn't seem like Democrats are going  to take over the Senate everybody should  vote consider every individual race  fifty-fifty but the numbers are not  looking great for Democrats taking over  the Senate but that's okay because if  you take over the house number one you  upend the entire legislative agenda of  Republicans and Trump  that's huge number one number two the  house has oversight over the executive  branch and has the power to do all sorts  of investigations that might actually go  somewhere and there's much more than  just Donald Trump to investigate to be  perfectly frank with you Trump's cabinet  is an extraordinarily corrupt greedy  self-aggrandizing group of people that  we need to be looking at very closely  winning state houses and governor's  races on Tuesday could deflate a ton of  trumps climate change craziness because  governors and state legislatures have a  ton of say about how their states will  deal with the environment but you've got  a vote whether you see it as a  referendum on Trump whether you see it  as a way to protect Robert Muller  whether you see it as a way to get  trumps cronies in the House and Senate I  don't care why you do it but you have to  vote and not be distracted by issues  that  are important but they're not going to  get resolved between now and Election  Day that's the really important thing  today's program sponsored in part by  Blink is comm slash Pakman I've talked  about blinkers before it's this awesome  app that I've been using for several  months now and what it does is take the  best and most critically acclaimed  non-fiction books and condenses them  into 15-minute audiobooks that you can  listen to in one sitting you could  listen to ten books in an afternoon I  know that many in our audience want to  expand their horizons and learn more  about all sorts of different topics but  we're mostly limited by time to some  degree I know I'm not able to read all  of the books that I want simply because  I've got other stuff going on and that's  why blink is - such a great tool you can  absorb the most important information  and insights from the book in one  sitting and our audience can get a seven  day free trial by going to blink accom  slash Pakman if you're watching on  youtube click the link in the video  description and after that free trial if  you like blinka stand i think you are  going to like it  you can continue enjoying thousands of  condensed audiobooks for about five  bucks a month go to be li NK is t.com  slash PA k ma n
 

